      "description": "Watch Peterborough United vs Sheffield Wednesday highlights and goals from League One on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 5, 2026. A Gritty Contest in League One Peterborough United and Sheffield Wednesday faced off in a highly anticipated League One clash that promised high drama from the first whistle. Both sets of supporters were treated to a physical and tactical battle as each side searched for a way to break the opposition's resolve. First Half Misfortune On 2026-09-05 , the match began with an early tactical shift for the hosts when Thomas O'Connor was forced off after just 14 minutes, replaced by David Okagbue . The deadlock was eventually broken in the 38th minute, but in unfortunate circumstances for the home side. Josh Feeney inadvertently turned the ball into his own net, giving Sheffield Wednesday the lead. The intensity grew before the break, leading to a yellow card for Ethan Williams as both teams battled for control. Quick Response and Growing Tension Peterborough United came out flying in the second half and found an equalizer almost immediately. In the 47th minute, James Dornelly turned provider for Ben Woods , who struck gold to level the score at 1-1. The game became increasingly cagey as the clock ticked on, with Jaden Heskey and Callum Slattery both entering the referee's book for the visitors. Multiple substitutions followed as both managers looked for a tactical edge in the closing stages. Valery Seals the Points The decisive moment arrived in the 79th minute. Kieran Morrison played a brilliant ball into the path of Yan Valery , who clinical finish restored the lead for Sheffield Wednesday . Despite a frantic finish and a late yellow card for Morrison in stoppage time, the visitors held their nerve through eight minutes of added time to secure a hard-fought victory."
